# ---- the game's own multiballs (item 164): the framework's count of the balls in play (The Beatles 1.29
# 0x1fd194, found here by its code); two or more is a multiball
site balls_in_play         0x0036aa88 0xe92d4010 0xe3014350
# Insider Connected score gate (item 166): the request header constructor (the endpoint in r1) and the
# message-begin thunk every sender calls next; the runtime refuses the score reports there
# (MODE_SDK.md, "Insider Connected: no score leaves a machine that carries modes")
site agent_header     0x00536120 0xe92d40f8 0xe2505000
site agent_begin      0x00540a7c 0xe590c004 0xe1a00001

# ---- the game's own modes (item 165): the framework's LIVE RECORDS. Every timed mode's start begins by
# asking 0x2b9290(lo, hi) whether one of its own records is alive (a walk of the list at [0x6fe9508]: u16 id at +0,
# next at +0x84) and refuses to start while one is; asked by the runtime, it says the mode is running.
# Each mode's ids are read off its start (or the function reading its timer adjustment) in the stock table.
# Metallica: the table's audit labels do not follow the ids (0xc8a58 counts two songs' audits, and a
# collect-select audit is counted where the next record is created), so each is named "a song mode".
# The first starts take no argument and create the record themselves (0xc5248 -> 182, 0xc7834 -> 187).
site live_records          0x002b9290 0xe3092508 0xe34026fe
value mode_records_1       0x00b800b6      # a song mode: ids 182..184
text mode_records_name_1   a song mode
value mode_records_2       0x00bd00bb      # a song mode: ids 187..189
text mode_records_name_2   a song mode
value mode_records_3       0x00c200c0      # a song mode: ids 192..194
text mode_records_name_3   a song mode
value mode_records_4       0x00e100df      # a song mode: ids 223..225
text mode_records_name_4   a song mode
value mode_records_5       0x00e800e7      # a song mode: ids 231..232
text mode_records_name_5   a song mode


# ---- a multiball of the mode's own (item 167): the framework's start-a-multiball (The Beatles 1.29
# 0x1fd310, found here by its code, 24/24 words alike): serve balls until r0 are in play, r1 0, r2 the
# ball save in ticks (62 a second), r3 0xbb as this build's own multiballs pass it, two zero words on the
# stack. pm_multiball_start / pm_multiball_add; a mode file's `multiball` line; the tab's Multiball.
site multiball_serve       0x0036ac04 0xe92d41f0 0xe306e956
# EMU 2026-09-26 (mb_batch.sh): served 3 on a mode file's start, both jackpot shots paid, add-a-ball to 4, drains 4-3-2-1, END (one ball left). PROVEN.

